    fix: a decimal disk floor is never truncated down. Addresses CF-082.
    
    scripts/disk_floor.py parsed a decimal floor with int(float(...)) (:67) and
    int(raw) for floats (:55), so "5.9G" resolved to 5 GiB. The --explain payload
    still said source "cli", so the substitution was invisible in the very output
    meant to make the floor falsifiable, and require_disk admitted a host that was
    below the number the operator wrote.
    
    parse_value now keeps the decimal: the value is parsed as a float, checked
    against MIN_GIB/MAX_GIB on that float, and returned as an int only when it is
    integral. So "5G" is still 5 (JSON number and bare print, no 5.0), "5.9G" is
    5.9, and "5.1G"/"5.5G"/"5.9G" are three distinct floors rather than one. The
    bounds now refuse 0.5G and 4096.5G, and a non-finite float (nan/inf) is a named
    FloorError instead of an int() crash.
    
    lib.sh needed no change: require_disk already compares with awk float math.
    Verified end to end with a df shim reporting exactly 5.5 GB free — floor 5.1 GB
    prints "PASS  disk — 5.5 GB free (floor 5.1 GB)", floor 5.9 GB prints
    "FAIL  disk — 5.5 GB free < floor 5.9 GB at /home/kara".
    
    Tests: tests/test_disk_floor.py replaces the test that pinned the truncation
    with decimal-preservation, integral-stays-int, three-distinct-decimals,
    never-below-requested, decimal-bounds and non-finite arms, plus a rung-by-rung
    decimal test (cli/env/config-role/config-default). It FAILS on the pre-fix
    module — 5 failures + 1 error, "Ran 18 tests ... FAILED" — and passes on this
    tree. tests/selftest.sh section 12 now runs the same probe at the admission
    layer against the 5.5 GB df shim, asserts both literal rows, and re-runs the
    deafbc3 resolver from git as a control that prints floor_gib 5.
    
    Docs: the module docstring (:17-22) states that decimals are preserved and
    integral values stay whole; specs/NODE.md and examples/floor.toml.example no
    longer call the values "whole GiB"; docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md §12 names CF-082.
    
    Evidence: bash tests/selftest.sh -> "SELFTEST: PASS" (rc 0);
    bash scripts/boardctl validate -> "RESULT: OK (7 warning(s))" (the warnings are
    pre-existing board rows); bash docs/audits/cf198-section-mapping.sh ->
    "arms_plan=58 arms_tree=58", "RESULT: OK".
    
    Residual, deliberately untouched: docs/handbook/appendices/units/11-* still
    records the truncation as a measured defect (its line-locator citations were
    already stale and this row does not re-derive that document); the same file's
    "accepted grammar" row is still accurate.
